            "block_content": "\"In no event shall the requirements of paragraph (1) be treated as met if the aggregate actual contributions for medical benefits (other than contributions with respect to collectively bargained retiree health liabilities within the meaning of section 420(e)(6)), when added to actual contributions for life insurance protection under the plan, exceed 25 percent of the total actual contributions to the plan (other than contributions to fund past service credits) after the date on which the account is established.\"",
